Third-party work and where this project came from
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

1. CodeX - https://github.com/dulapahv/CodeX
   Copyright (c) Dulapah Vibulsanti. Licensed under AGPL-3.0.

   VEXCollab was written after studying CodeX and takes its product idea
   directly: a no-sign-up, link-shareable, real-time collaborative code editor
   built on Monaco and Yjs. The source here was written fresh rather than
   forked - different architecture (single Next.js app with an in-process
   Socket.IO relay, rather than a pnpm/Turborepo split client and server) and a
   different purpose (VEX V5 robotics). VEXCollab is nonetheless released under
   AGPL-3.0, the same license as CodeX, so that the lineage stays honest and
   nothing is taken from that project's community.

2. v5-serial-protocol - https://github.com/Jerrylum/v5-serial-protocol
   Copyright (c) 2022 Jerry Lum. Licensed under MIT.

   Vendored verbatim (plus one `@ts-nocheck` pragma per file) into
   src/lib/v5-serial-protocol/. That directory carries its own LICENSE and a
   VENDORED.md explaining the details. MIT permits this and is compatible with
   AGPL-3.0.

